  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.084,
            0.743,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the differences in the properties of water in solid, liquid and gaseous states?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.126,
            0.743,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ice (solid state)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " retains its shape irrespective of the container in which it is placed while water takes the shape of the container. Ice does not flow or spread."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.188,
            0.744,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water (liquid state)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " flows and changes its shape. Water does not have a fixed shape. It takes up the shape of the container in which it is kept, but the volume of water remains constant. Does water also possess the property to spread? Yes, water also has the property to spread while keeping the volume constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.314,
            0.744,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water vapour (gaseous state)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " exhibits a property of spreading out in the entire available space. Gases do not possess a fixed shape. Water vapour exists even at room temperature; though it is invisible to us. It is present in the air around us. The water that evaporates during processes like drying of clothes or mopping of floors contribute to the water vapour in the air around us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.46,
            0.743,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You are now familiar with the three states of water. Some other substances also exhibit these states. For example, wax, oil and ghee. Let us look at some more examples of solids, liquids and gases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.543,
            0.742,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look around and find some examples of solid substances. Some examples could be stones, wood and glass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.585,
            0.743,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the other examples of liquids you can think of? Here are two examples—milk and oil. Think of five more examples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.647,
            0.744,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Have you ever noticed that you can smell the food being cooked even without entering the kitchen? How does this smell reach us?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.709,
            0.743,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is because the smell of yummy food from cooking spreads through the air and reaches our nostrils, even if we are not in the kitchen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.772,
            0.743,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the other examples of gases you can think of? What about oxygen and carbon dioxide?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.827,
            0.726,
            0.852
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.4 How can we change the States of Water?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.863,
            0.744,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So far we have learnt that water can exist in solid, liquid and gaseous states. How can you change the state of water?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.889,
            0.697,
            0.91,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Journey through States of Water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 13,
